1
00:00:00,438 --> 00:00:02,290
Vienna, eighteen sixty five.

2
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:05,220
A doctor is led into an asylum.

3
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:07,540
There, it is said, the guards beat him.

4
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:09,410
Two weeks later he is dead.

5
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:15,700
I see a time when only cases of self-infec
tion will occur in the maternity hospitals

6
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,660
of the world.

7
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:18,570
Ignaz Semmelweis wrote that.

8
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:21,740
But most doctors of his day rejected it.

9
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:25,410
In his day, every doctor
knew what killed new mothers:

10
00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:26,430
bad air.

11
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:29,550
So why did they die in one
clinic of Vienna's hospital,

12
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:31,800
and hardly at all in the next?

13
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,810
Vienna, eighteen forty six.

14
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:38,470
Semmelweis, twenty eight, is the
new assistant in the First Clinic.

15
00:00:38,470 --> 00:00:41,270
Here, doctors and students
deliver the babies.

16
00:00:41,398 --> 00:00:43,520
Next door, midwives do.

17
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:46,230
That year, one mother in nine dies here.

18
00:00:46,406 --> 00:00:49,060
Next door, one in thirty six.

19
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:51,700
Yet both clinics share one hospital,

20
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:53,220
and the same Vienna air.

21
00:00:53,776 --> 00:00:54,981
Everything was in question.

22
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:59,380
Only the large number of deaths
was an unquestionable reality.

23
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:01,050
But the women know the difference.

24
00:01:01,509 --> 00:01:01,820
Please.

25
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:03,530
Not the first clinic.

26
00:01:03,530 --> 00:01:06,280
He wrote that they knelt,
wringing their hands,

27
00:01:06,330 --> 00:01:07,960
begging to be sent next door.

28
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:10,500
So Semmelweis tests every explanation,

29
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:11,440
one by one.

30
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:13,520
The mothers deliver on their side,

31
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:14,573
as the midwives do.

32
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:15,950
Nothing changes.

33
00:01:16,430 --> 00:01:17,430
But there is the bell.

34
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:20,250
A priest crosses the ward to the dying,

35
00:01:20,303 --> 00:01:22,250
an attendant ringing ahead of him.

36
00:01:22,506 --> 00:01:26,490
Even to me myself it had a
strange effect upon my nerves,

37
00:01:26,522 --> 00:01:29,370
when I heard the bell hurry past my door.

38
00:01:29,370 --> 00:01:31,560
He sends the priest a quieter way.

39
00:01:31,627 --> 00:01:33,480
Still, the mothers die.

40
00:01:33,566 --> 00:01:36,110
Then, in March eighteen forty seven,

41
00:01:36,150 --> 00:01:41,630
Semmelweis's friend Jakob Kolletschka is c
ut by a student's knife during an autopsy,

42
00:01:41,650 --> 00:01:42,570
and dies.

43
00:01:42,610 --> 00:01:46,990
Day and night I was haunted by the
image of Kolletschka's disease.

44
00:01:46,990 --> 00:01:50,480
But Kolletschka's body shows the
same disease as the dying mothers.

45
00:01:50,566 --> 00:01:54,110
And the students who cut the dead
walk straight on to the mothers.

46
00:01:54,282 --> 00:01:56,000
What are their hands carrying?
